            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 0.8 (build 751)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Compare sizes each side on its own.</b> Side by side shows both pictures at the same height, stacked at the same width, each at its own aspect ratio &#8212; a tall 9:16 beside a wide 16:9 is no longer small. Marks, aspect guides and frame grabs follow.</li>
<li><b>Anamorphic desqueeze.</b> Color &#9656; Anamorphic Desqueeze (or right-click the picture): 1.25&#215; to 2&#215;, per clip, with Apply to All Clips. The picture, marks, guides, compare and frame grabs all use the desqueezed shape; Clip info shows both aspects. Movie exports are not desqueezed yet.</li>
<li>Camera raw from RED and Blackmagic is named for what it is.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
